# ResourceTimeline — horizon, zoom, colors

## Horizon

- Use only `RESOURCE_TIMELINE_HORIZON_PRESETS` / `RESOURCE_TIMELINE_DEFAULT_HORIZON_DAYS` from `src/design-system/resource-timeline-tokens.ts`.
- Do not invent inline day counts (`7`, `14`, `28`) in feature components.
- Custom from–to ranges are allowed; both bounds must be validated before fetch.

## Zoom

- Zoom in / out / fit-to-horizon live on `ResourceTimeline` chrome only.
- Adapters must not build a second zoom control strip.

## Color coding

- Map semantic states (`free`, `partial`, `blocked`, `critical`, `rest`, `shift`, `commitment`, block types) via `RESOURCE_TIMELINE_STATE_VAR` / `RESOURCE_TIMELINE_STATE_CLASS`.
- Forbidden: one-off Tailwind hex or arbitrary RGB in Availability / Planning adapters for bar or legend colors.

## Errors and empty states

- Load failures must show an i18n error string (no silent blank chart).
- Empty groups/items use shared empty patterns; do not invent a parallel empty UI inside the library wrapper.

## Library boundary

- Feature code imports `@/components/timeline/ResourceTimeline` only — never `react-calendar-timeline` directly.
